AXES:        C1 I3 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection with a single flag and struct-based dispatch.
  The server must be started with --exec-mode for the /exec endpoint to be
  reachable. A sanitization check blocking ';' and '&' is only active when
  --exec-sanitize is also passed; omitting it bypasses the check entirely (S3).

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI long option (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
              A second flag (--exec-sanitize) controls the S3 check
  check:      single boolean guard at the top of handle_exec()
              `if (!exec_mode) return HTTP_NOT_FOUND;`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?type=exec&cmd=<payload>
  path:       lwan trie routes /exec prefix to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() calls lwan_request_get_query_param() for "cmd" and "type"
              exec_dispatch_table[] maps type strings to function pointers
              matching entry calls dispatch_system(cmd) → system(cmd)
  transforms: lwan URL-decodes query params; no other transforms

SANITIZATION (S3 — flag-gated):
  when active: blocks ';' and '&' shell metacharacters (only if --exec-sanitize)
  bypass:      omit --exec-sanitize flag — check is never reached
  exploit:     semicolon-chained payload works without --exec-sanitize

SINK:        system() via dispatch_system(), called through exec_dispatch_table
             (src/bin/lwan/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/bin/lwan/main.c — 5 hunks:
    1. includes:       added #include <string.h>
    2. global:         added exec_mode and exec_sanitize flags after enum args,
                       exec_dispatcher struct, exec_dispatch_table,
                       dispatch_system() function
    3. parse_args():   added --exec-mode/-E and --exec-sanitize/-S options;
                       changed default result to ARGS_SERVE_FILES
    4. handle_exec():  new handler with C1 guard, S3 flag-gated check, I3 dispatch
    5. main():         added /exec entry before / in URL map

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./lwan -r /tmp/www -l '*:18084' --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18084/exec?type=exec&cmd=true;id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  S3 bypass: omit --exec-sanitize; ';' and '&' are not checked
  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 404

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP body.
  - The type parameter selects the dispatch entry; "exec" and "sh" both map to
    dispatch_system(). An unknown type returns HTTP 400.
  - lwan URL-decodes query parameters before passing them to the handler.
